+# UC16 create record design
+
+Intent: issue17 UC16, FR-RC-01, BR08/09; create only client-encrypted account-owned records, validate permitted relationships and return public metadata. All AF01–05 must be covered. Existing unattended batch authorization replaces repeated stage menus, not tests/review/CI. Independent protocol/client approvals remain development-only deferred/release-gated.
+
+Preferred design uses existing VaultRecord/FolderId/ProfileRecord schema and native EncryptedEnvelope, no new migrations/dependencies/crypto/templates. POST /api/records strict required recordId/envelope/editedAt/profileIds plus optional nullable folderId. Only metadata output recordId/revision/serverSequence/editedAt, initial revision1 and global safe sequence; normalizeUTCtimestamps down to microseconds beforePGbinding inclpre2000, minimum10ticks. GUIDs canonical atHTTP, arraysunique/nonzero; initialresourceepoch1. Owner from currentidentity/account, neverbody. Encrypted name, text/numeric/boolean/hidden-text and template requirements remain caller-side inside ciphertext.
+
+Account-wide current opaque access can create unlinked records or link to multiple own active profiles and optional own active folder. Selected access can create NEW owned content only inside its own selection: profileIds must contain exactly its selected profile, optional folder must already lie in that selection's direct folder/owned descendant scope. Empty selectedprofileIds403; otherprofile/outofscopefolder404; no existing content attached to wider scope. New directly linked record is then visible inside selection. Recipients cannot create resources for another owner, even with write grants; collection membership belongs its specified later UC. Alternative account-wide-only recordcreation would prevent standalone profile-password users from creating content; accepting arbitrary profile IDs with a selected handle would broaden authority.
+
+TX account→session→ownedprofile rows publicGUIDorder→ownedfolder/ancestors. Current active account/nonterminal and valid session policy/generation/lifetime/selected-current-active-profile mandatory. Account lock serializes all ownedwriters; do not lock foreign owners. Resolve onlycurrent owned active targets, preserve hidden404 before malformedstoredcounter/disclosure. Optionalfolderancestor walk checks sameowner/active/nonterminal at eachstep, detects cycliccorrupt ancestry failclosed503; no client-supplied internalIDs. Recheck session afterwaits beforetarget/duplicate details. Parentcounterpositive safe, saturation409; reserved recordID(existing/trash/terminal)409, concurrentduplicatesonewinner. Existing globalResourceId-only terminal collision remains separate required fix before ANYphysicalpurge; conservatively reserve existingterminal IDs until repaired, active IDs of different kinds remain permitted.
+
+Final conditionalSQL insert rechecks account/session/currentpolicygen/selectedscope/folder+profilelifecycle at statement_timestamp (exclusiveexpiry). Insert record and direct profilelinks, increment affectedprofile revisions/sequences/stamps without touching ciphertext/wrappers/EditedAt, likewise optionalparentfolderstructuralrevision/sequence, inoneTX. No replace-existing sets. No parent expectedrevisions required because creation is an additive commutative operation under ownership locks, not replacement of a cached set; existing expectedrevision writers observe metadata advances and conflict normally. No extra metadata for profiles affected only through dynamicdescendants: directlinks change onlyspecifiedprofiles, future recordlist/sync must evaluate currentcontainment. Any failure afterinsert/link/parentupdate rollsback all; unique/exhaustedsequence409, corruptpersistence503, retry creates once. No accesssession/challenge changes.
